From: Monea Software <build@hdsatelit.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] GStreamer: punch the video hole when painting without compositing

The hole-punch rendering relies on the compositor: the video layer carries
a hole-punch buffer that clears the area and sends the rectangle to the
sink. When the page is painted without accelerated compositing (CPU-only
rendering, as on receivers whose GPU cannot run the compositor), there is
no layer and nothing reaches the sink.

When the hole-punch quirk asks for it (GStreamerHolePunchQuirk::
paintsVideoHole()), the player sends the video rectangle, in CSS pixels of
the page, when the video element paints, and clears the area (alpha 0) so
that the video plane under the graphics shows through. Once the hole-punch
sink exists, the element is painted again.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [satellite receiver configuration]

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
@@ -4319,6 +4319,25 @@
     if (!m_pageIsVisible || isSuspended())
         return;
 
+    if (isHolePunchRenderingEnabled() && !m_quirksManagerForTesting) {
+        // Without accelerated compositing there is no hole-punch layer. The video rectangle, in CSS pixels of the
+        // page, goes to the quirk from here, and the area is cleared (alpha 0) so that the video plane under the
+        // graphics shows through.
+        auto& quirksManager = GStreamerQuirksManager::singleton();
+        if (auto clearsHole = quirksManager.paintsVideoHole()) {
+            float scale = 1;
+            if (RefPtr player = m_player.get())
+                scale = player->playerContentsScale();
+            auto pageRect = context.getCTM(GraphicsContext::DefinitelyIncludeDeviceScale).mapRect(rect);
+            if (scale > 0 && scale != 1)
+                pageRect.scale(1 / scale);
+            quirksManager.setHolePunchVideoRectangle(m_videoSink.get(), enclosingIntRect(pageRect));
+            if (*clearsHole)
+                context.clearRect(rect);
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+
     // Keep a reference to the sample to avoid keeping the sampleMutex locked, which would be prone
     // to deadlocks if triggerRepaint is called while the video frame converter is blocked on its
     // state change.
@@ -4559,6 +4578,11 @@
         m_videoSink = createHolePunchVideoSink();
         // Do not check the m_videoSink value. The nullptr case will trigger auto-plugging in playbin.
         pushNextHolePunchBuffer();
+        // Without compositing the hole is made when the element paints: paint it again now that the sink exists.
+        if (!m_quirksManagerForTesting && GStreamerQuirksManager::singleton().paintsVideoHole()) {
+            if (RefPtr player = m_player.get())
+                player->repaint();
+        }
         return m_videoSink.get();
     }
 
